<title>PERU: European Union to donate $42.5 million to Peru.</title>
<headline>European Union to donate $42.5 million to Peru.</headline>
<dateline>JANGAS, Peru 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Alberto Fujimori said Thursday the European Union had agreed to donate $42.5 million for anti-poverty projects in Peru.</p>
<p>During a visit to the highland region of Ancash, Fujimori said $21 million of the loan would be invested in development projects in that zone, and $21.5 million in other parts of the country.</p>
<p>He added that the government would contribute another $18 million to the same projects.</p>
<p>-- Renzo Pipoli, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
